In triangle $ABC,$ $D$ lies on $\overline{BC}$ extended past $C$ such that $BD:DC = 3:1,$ and $E$ lies on $\overline{AC}$ such that $AE:EC = 5:3.$  Let $P$ be the intersection of lines $BE$ and $AD.$

[asy]
unitsize(0.8 cm);

pair A, B, C, D, E, F, P;

A = (1,4);
B = (0,0);
C = (6,0);
D = interp(B,C,3/2);
E = interp(A,C,5/8);
P = extension(A,D,B,E);

draw(A--B--C--cycle);
draw(A--D--C);
draw(B--P);

label("$A$", A, N);
label("$B$", B, SW);
label("$C$", C, S);
label("$D$", D, SE);
label("$E$", E, S);
label("$P$", P, NE);
[/asy]

